.TH CANTCPD 8 "2026-09-28" "cantcp" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
cantcpd \- cantcp SocketCAN-to-TCP gateway daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cantcpd
[\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cantcpd
bridges one Linux SocketCAN interface and TCP clients speaking the cantcp
protocol: frames read from the CAN bus are broadcast to every connected
client, frames sent by the clients are written to the bus. The connection is
either plain (trusted perimeter) or TLS 1.3; plain mode listens on the
loopback interface unless
.B \-\-allow-plain
is given.
.PP
Settings come from the built-in defaults, the JSON configuration file, the
.B CANTCP_*
environment variables and the command line flags, in that order of
precedence. Every value is validated before the daemon starts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIpath\fR
JSON configuration file. Default:
.IR /etc/cantcp/cantcpd.json ;
a missing default file is not an error.
.TP
.B \-\-listen \fIhost:port\fR
TCP listen address (default
.IR 127.0.0.1:29536 ).
.TP
.B \-\-can \fIinterface\fR
SocketCAN interface to serve (default
.IR can0 ).
One daemon instance serves one interface: run one instance per bus with its
own unit instance and configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-error-frames
Forward CAN error frames.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-plain
Allow plain mode on a non-loopback address. Without TLS settings and this
flag the daemon refuses to start on a public address.
.TP
.B \-\-tls-cert \fIfile\fR, \fB\-\-tls-key \fIfile\fR
TLS server certificate and key. Setting both enables TLS 1.3.
.TP
.B \-\-tls-ca \fIfile\fR
CA file used to verify client certificates.
.TP
.B \-\-tls-client-auth \fImode\fR
Client certificate mode:
.IR none ,
.I verify_if_given
or
.IR require_and_verify .
.TP
.B \-\-max-connections \fIn\fR
Maximum number of simultaneous clients (default 16).
.TP
.B \-\-client-queue \fIn\fR
Per-client frame queue length (default 1024). When the queue is full the
frame is dropped and counted.
.TP
.B \-\-read-timeout \fId\fR, \fB\-\-write-timeout \fId\fR
TLS handshake timeout and per-frame write timeout (default 5s each).
.TP
.B \-\-idle-timeout \fId\fR
Close a client after this idle time; 0 disables it.
.TP
.B \-\-max-frames-per-second \fIn\fR
Per-client frame rate limit from the client to the CAN bus; 0 disables it.
.TP
.B \-\-stats-listen \fIhost:port\fR
HTTP statistics address (default
.IR 127.0.0.1:29537 ).
.TP
.B \-\-no-stats
Disable the HTTP statistics listener.
.TP
.B \-\-log-level \fIlevel\fR, \fB\-\-log-format \fIformat\fR
Log level (debug, info, warn, error) and format (text, json).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
The JSON file accepts the keys
.IR listen ,
.IR allow_plain ,
.IR can ,
.IR tls ,
.IR limits ,
.I stats
and
.IR log .
Unknown keys are rejected. Durations are Go strings such as
.IR 5s .
See
.I /usr/share/doc/cantcpd/examples/
and the project documentation for the complete schema.
.SH HTTP ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B GET /healthz
Liveness check.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/stats
JSON statistics snapshot: CAN counters, TCP counters and the client list.
.TP
.B GET /metrics
Prometheus text exposition format.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the TLS certificate material, the log level and the limits from the
same configuration sources. The listen address, the CAN interface, the TLS
switch and the statistics address are fixed for the lifetime of the process.
.SH SECURITY
TLS is limited to version 1.3. The daemon never logs frame payloads. The
systemd unit runs as the unprivileged user
.I cantcp
with the single capability CAP_NET_RAW and with a hardened sandbox
(ProtectSystem=strict, PrivateTmp, RestrictAddressFamilies, SystemCallFilter).
See the project SECURITY.md for the threat model.
.SH CROSS-COMPILATION
The binaries are pure Go. Build them on any platform for any Go target:
.PP
.nf
CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./cmd/cantcpd
CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm64 go build ./cmd/cantcpd
CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm GOARM=7 go build ./cmd/cantcpd
.fi
.PP
The published release packages use linux/amd64, linux/arm64 and linux/armv7
(GOARM=7, the Debian armhf architecture).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cantcp-cli (1),
.I https://github.com/burn-lab-dev/cantcp
